Patch of TDLib sources needed by the Bot API server metrics.

- Adds the method getMemoryObjectCounts, which returns numbers of objects of different types stored in memory by
  a TDLib instance, which are never deleted from memory, or are deleted only after some time.
  The counts are calculated in constant time, except for the number of loaded messages, which is maintained by
  MessagesManager in loaded_message_count_.
- Allows bots to use getStorageStatisticsFast.

The patch is applied automatically by CMake. See td-patches/README.md.

diff --git a/td/generate/scheme/td_api.tl b/td/generate/scheme/td_api.tl
index 1a23165..06402c4 100644
--- a/td/generate/scheme/td_api.tl
+++ b/td/generate/scheme/td_api.tl
@@ -9800,6 +9800,12 @@ storageStatistics size:int53 count:int32 by_chat:vector<storageStatisticsByChat>
 //@log_size Size of the TDLib internal log
 storageStatisticsFast files_size:int53 file_count:int32 database_size:int53 language_pack_database_size:int53 log_size:int53 = StorageStatisticsFast;
 
+//@description Contains the number of objects of a type, which are stored in memory @type Type of the objects @count Number of the objects
+memoryObjectCount type:string count:int53 = MemoryObjectCount;
+
+//@description Contains numbers of objects of different types, which are stored in memory @counts Numbers of objects
+memoryObjectCounts counts:vector<memoryObjectCount> = MemoryObjectCounts;
+
 //@description Contains database statistics
 //@statistics Database statistics in an unspecified human-readable format
 databaseStatistics statistics:string = DatabaseStatistics;
@@ -15783,6 +15789,9 @@ getStorageStatistics chat_limit:int32 = StorageStatistics;
 //@description Quickly returns approximate storage usage statistics. Can be called before authorization
 getStorageStatisticsFast = StorageStatisticsFast;
 
+//@description Returns numbers of objects of different types, which are stored in memory. The objects are never deleted from memory, or deleted only after some time
+getMemoryObjectCounts = MemoryObjectCounts;
+
 //@description Returns database statistics
 getDatabaseStatistics = DatabaseStatistics;
 
